\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The bar is conjugation}
\date{2026-11-13}

\p{The bar #{\overline\lambda} is complex conjugation, extended to the
declared involution of the ground ring. Mathematical physics writes
#{\bar z} or #{z^*}. Geometric calculus uses the overbar for the
adjoint function, which here is #{A^\dagger}. The law of this
definition is
##{(\lambda a)^\dagger=\overline\lambda\, a^\dagger.}
A bar that means closure, or a modified copy, is not this involution.}
